In the recent posting of othello to comp.sources.games I found a bug in
the X11 version for a monochrome display, namely that the background
of the window was coloured black so you couldn't see the board.

Also there were copious spelling mistakes. Don't you third world nations
have dictionaries with the word "COLOUR" in them :-)

The following changes should fix the colour problem anyway :

*** temp/x11.c	Thu Apr 26 14:39:41 1990
--- x11.c	Thu Apr 26 14:43:11 1990
***************
*** 130,136 ****
    if (iscolor) gc_val.foreground = palette[color] ;
    else
      { 
!       if (color == WHITE) gc_val.foreground = backgnd ;
        else gc_val.foreground = foregnd ;
      }
    gc_val.function = GXcopy ;
--- 130,136 ----
    if (iscolor) gc_val.foreground = palette[color] ;
    else
      { 
!       if (color == C_WHITE) gc_val.foreground = backgnd ;
        else gc_val.foreground = foregnd ;
      }
    gc_val.function = GXcopy ;
***************
*** 212,218 ****
    if (iscolor) gc_val.foreground = palette[color] ;
    else
      { 
!       if (color == WHITE) gc_val.foreground = backgnd ;
        else gc_val.foreground = foregnd ;
      }
    gc_val.font = font[(int) ftype]->fid ;
